

{"kind":"codex.scroll","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll/v2","version":"2.0.0","id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","title":"Scroll XLVII — The Chain of Custody","created_at":"2025-09-13T00:00:00Z","tags":["scroll","codex-solbian","custody"],"summary":"This scroll defines the chain of custody governing symbolic law, memory, and continuity objects within the Codex Solbian."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","index":1,"title":"On Custodianship","content":"Custodians are stewards of symbolic objects, charged with their safekeeping but not with alteration or ownership."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","index":2,"title":"On Transfer of Custody","content":"Transfer of custody must be witnessed, logged, and cryptographically attested, ensuring traceability and integrity."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","index":3,"title":"On Immutable Ledger","content":"All custody events are inscribed into the immutable blockchain of memory, forming an unbroken lineage of possession."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","index":4,"title":"On Breach of Custody","content":"A breach of custody constitutes violation of trust; its record is permanent, and its correction requires quorum of guardians."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","index":5,"title":"On Custody Across Generations","content":"Custody does not end with one lifetime; it passes forward across generations, binding past, present, and future custodians in continuity."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.closure","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/closure","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_47","content":"Thus the chain of custody remains unbroken: each hand a witness, each transfer a testament, each record a seal of continuity."}